== Mechanics ==
'''Sea Creatures''' are mobs which can be caught while fishing. The type of Sea Creature which is caught depends on the player's {{Skill|Fishing}} level, the bobber location and fishing medium ({{Item|Water}} or {{Item|Lava}}). When killed, they drop loot and {{Skill|Fishing}} XP.
* The list of all Sea Creatures, their requirements to be caught and drops can be seen in the in-game Sea Creature Guide through the Fishing Skill menu or the <code>/scg</code> command.
* The chance in percentage to catch a Sea Creature is determined by the player's {{Stat|scc}}. The chance of catching a Sea Creature is reduced on {{Zone|Private Island}} and {{Zone|The Garden}} though this change is not reflected in the [[Stats]] menu.
* Sea Creatures cannot be damaged by arrows, except those shot from the {{Item|Prismarine Bow}}. They take {{green|2x}} damage from [[Fishing Rods]].
*There is a Sea Creature cap of {{green|60}} per server ({{green|30}} on {{Zone|Galatea}}{{Confirm}}). After this cap is reached, players will only be able to catch {{cyan|fish}} and {{gold|treasure}}, even with {{stat|scc|100}}, until some Sea Creatures are killed or despawn. Furthermore, there is a per-player Sea Creature cap of {{green|10}} on all islands.
** If a player already has {{green|9}} Sea Creatures out and catches two at once due to {{Stat|Double Hook}}, this cap can be exceeded, making the theoretical maximum per player {{green|11}} Sea Creatures. However, {{MobSprite|Magma Slug;Magma Slugs}} and {{MobSprite|Water Hydra;Water Hydras}} are an exception. Despite being split up to multiple entities, it still only counts as {{green|one}} towards the cap.
** Upon reaching the cap, players will receive the following message: {{Dialogue|&cThere is not enough space for another Sea Creature! Kill some to make space for new ones!}}
* Sea Creatures despawn if not killed within {{green|6}} minutes, or if the player who fished them up leaves the server. The {{MobSprite|Magma Slug;Baby Magma Slug}} is an exception to this as  it does not despawn naturally after being split up to three.

